{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This site uses the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". One command and it works,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because this is a Swift package with a single target."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In bigger projects the setup is not that simple. An Xcode project with many","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets, a framework whose docs live in a separate folder, a site that also"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carries onboarding pages. In those cases the plugin is not enough and you have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to run "},{"code":"docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is how I do it. Every step is implemented in "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"small package that only exists to be documented, so you can read the real"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"files instead of my snippets."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-two-halves","text":"The two halves","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC can render two kinds of content."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Generated API reference.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Types and functions with their doc comments. You"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never write these pages. The compiler describes your module in a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", one JSON file per module, and DocC turns it into pages."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Manual documentation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Articles and guides you write as Markdown inside a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"documentation catalog","type":"text"}]},{"text":", a folder ending in ","type":"text"},{"code":".docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Alone, neither is enough. The API reference says what a function returns, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not why the feature exists. The guide explains the idea, but cannot link into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the code. Putting them together is one flag. The rest is the work around it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"1-Write-the-doc-comments","text":"1. Write the doc comments","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Generated pages are only as good as the comments in the code. A one line","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"summary, then details, then the parameters. Keep the summary to one sentence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because DocC reuses it as the subtitle in every list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only ","type":"text"},{"code":"public","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols end up in the symbol graph, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never show up on the website.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"anchor":"2-Add-a-catalog","type":"heading","text":"2. Add a catalog"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The catalog can live anywhere. It does not have to be inside a target, because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you pass its path to ","type":"text"},{"code":"docc","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["doc\/","└── GardenKit.docc\/","    ├── GardenKit.md      # landing page","    └── Guides\/"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"DocC flattens the catalog and finds pages by file name, so the folders are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only for your own order. Keep the file names unique.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One page becomes the front door. If you title a file with the module name in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"double backticks, DocC merges it into the generated module page:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes the overview and your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Topics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" groups set the order of everything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"below. That is what GardenKit and this site do.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Get-the-symbol-graphs","text":"3. Get the symbol graphs","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the generated half. Ask the compiler for symbol graphs while"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["xcodebuild build \\","    -scheme \"GardenKit\" \\","    -destination \"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator\" \\","    -derivedDataPath \"$build_dir\" \\","    -quiet \\","    OTHER_SWIFT_FLAGS=\"\\$(inherited) -emit-symbol-graph -emit-symbol-graph-dir $symbol_graphs_dir\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Three details matter here.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"generic\/platform=iOS Simulator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" builds for the simulator SDK without picking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"a device, so codesigning never runs. A docs job has nothing to s","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\\$(inherited)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps the flags the project already sets. If you drop it, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"module compiles differently and you will not notice right away."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"docbuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"xcodebuild docbuild","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" looks easier, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"documentation for the whole dependency tree. If one of those dependencies has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Objective-C headers, DocC’s header pass can fail with duplicate symbol errors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the build stops. A plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" never runs that pass. It on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift symbol graphs, which is all DocC needs. This took me a while to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"figure out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"4. Keep only your module","type":"heading","anchor":"4-Keep-only-your-module"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The build writes a graph for every module it compiled, including"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"dependencies. If you pass all of them to DocC, your dependencies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"your website:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["find \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" -type f -name '*.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit.symbols.json' \\","    ! -name 'GardenKit@*.symbols.json' \\","    -delete"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both patterns are needed. ","type":"text"},{"code":"GardenKit.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has your own symbols.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GardenKit@Foundation.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an extension graph, one per module you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extend. Delete those and every ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your code qui","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disappears from the site.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"5. Put them together","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"5-Put-them-together"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the command everything was preparing for:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["xcrun docc convert \"doc\/GardenKit.docc\" \\","    --additional-symbol-graph-dir \"$symbol_graphs_dir\" \\","    --fallback-display-name \"GardenKit\" \\","    --fallback-bundle-identifier \"com.example.gardenkit\" \\","    --output-dir \"$output_dir\" \\","    --transform-for-static-hosting \\","    --emit-digest"],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"--additional-symbol-graph-dir","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the flag that merges the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol links in your articles resolve because of it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two ","type":"text"},{"code":"--fallback-*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" options give DocC the metadata Xcode would normally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass for a target. A catalog you convert by hand has no target, so they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"required. ","type":"text"},{"code":"--transform-for-static-hosting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes the output serv","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file host, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--emit-digest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the index the search needs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While writing, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"preview","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":"convert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Same options,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost:8080","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and reloads when you save a Markdown file. It reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol graphs from the folder you already created, so there is no rebuild.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"6. Serve it","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"6-Serve-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the site is not at the root of the domain, pass the prefix or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"URL will be wrong:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["xcrun docc convert … --hosting-base-path \"docs\""],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DocC does not write a root page either, so add a redirect:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["echo '<script>window.location.href += \"documentation\/gardenkit\"<\/script>' \\","    > \"$output_dir\/index.html\""],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That is the whole pipeline. I keep it in a script with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"-o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fl","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the docs are previewed locally, with it they are converted for hosting. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full version is ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit\/blob\/main\/scripts\/generate_docs.sh"},{"text":". In CI the output is just a folder of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"static files, so publishing it is a copy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"text":"Common problems","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Common-problems"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"Topic reference 'Plant' couldn't be resolved.","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The symbol graphs did"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"not reach DocC. Check the path you passed, and that pruning did not delete","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your own graph."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Extensions are missing.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"Module@Other.symbols.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" graphs were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An internal type is missing."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Symbol graphs only contain public API.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"Links","text":"Links","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"GardenKit","type":"text"}],"overridingTitle":"GardenKit","type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit"},{"text":", the example, with the full script","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-symbolkit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", the symbol graph format"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPipeline","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/AsyncSequenceOperator","doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite"],"title":"Patch Notes","generated":true,"anchor":"Patch-Notes"}],"sampleCodeDownload":{"action":{"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"View GardenKit on GitHub","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit"},"kind":"sampleDownload"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpipeline"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Combining Generated and Manual Docs","roleHeading":"Article","images":[{"identifier":"card-docc.svg","type":"card"}],"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Haydar Karkin"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Building one documentation site from two sources: the API reference the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compiler generates, and the articles I write by hand.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes/DoccPersonalSite":{"url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes\/doccpersonalsite","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/DoccPersonalSite","kind":"article","title":"Turning DocC into a Personal Site","role":"article","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"card-site.svg"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a personal site actually needs, and how far DocC gets you with each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those things."}]},"https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-docc-plugin":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-docc-plugin","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-docc-plugin"}],"type":"link","title":"swift-docc-plugin"},"https://github.com/haydarKarkin/GardenKit":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin\/GardenKit","checksum":null,"type":"download"},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/formattinnt":{"type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Formatting your documentation content","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/formattinnt","title":"Formatting your documentation content"},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes/AsyncSequenceOperator":{"url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes\/asyncsequenceoperator","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/AsyncSequenceOperator","title":"Writing Your Own AsyncSequence Operator","kind":"article","role":"article","images":[{"identifier":"card-async.svg","type":"card"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"What it takes to add an operator like ","type":"text"},{"code":"throttleFirst","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how to test it without waiting for real time to pass.","type":"text"}]},"https://www.swift.org/documentation/docc/":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/","url":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/documentation\/docc\/","title":"DocC documentation","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"DocC documentation","type":"text"}]},"doc://ReleaseNotes/documentation/ReleaseNotes":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Senior iOS Developer. I build iOS apps that keep working as they grow."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Haydar Karkin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes","url":"\/documentation\/releasenotes"},"card-docc.svg":{"type":"image","alt":null,"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/ReleaseNotes\/card-docc.svg","s